    <content>
      <![CDATA[<div class="note blue icon-padding flat"><i class="note-icon fas fa-bullhorn"></i><p>This post is for Butterfly 4.0 and above. Some options may not be available in older versions.<br>If you are a new user, it is recommended to use the <a href="https://github.com/jerryc127/hexo-theme-butterfly/releases">latest release</a>.</p></div><h1 id="Install"><a href="#Install" class="headerlink" title="Install"></a>Install</h1><h2 id="Git-Installation"><a href="#Git-Installation" class="headerlink" title="Git Installation"></a>Git Installation</h2><div class="tabs"><div class="nav-tabs"><button type="button" class="tab active">Stable version (Recommended)</button><button type="button" class="tab">Dev version (Testing)</button></div><div class="tab-contents"><div class="tab-item-content active"><figure class="highlight bash"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line">git <span class="built_in">clone</span> -b master https://github.com/jerryc127/hexo-theme-butterfly.git themes/butterfly</span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure></div><div class="tab-item-content"><blockquote><p>Dev version may contain bugs. It is not recommended unless you know what you are doing.</p></blockquote><figure class="highlight bash"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line">git <span class="built_in">clone</span> -b dev https://github.com/jerryc127/hexo-theme-butterfly.git themes/butterfly</span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure></div></div><div class="tab-to-top"><button type="button" aria-label="scroll to top"><i class="fas fa-arrow-up"></i></button></div></div><p>If you want to upgrade the theme, run the following command in the <code>themes/butterfly</code> directory:</p><figure class="highlight bash"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line">git pull</span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure><h2 id="NPM-Installation"><a href="#NPM-Installation" class="headerlink" title="NPM Installation"></a>NPM Installation</h2><blockquote><p>Requires Hexo 5.0.0 and above</p></blockquote><figure class="highlight bash"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line">npm install hexo-theme-butterfly</span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure><div class="note warning flat"><p>When installing via npm, the theme files will be placed in <code>node_modules/hexo-theme-butterfly</code> rather than the <code>themes/</code> folder.</p></div><p>If you want to upgrade the theme:</p><figure class="highlight bash"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line">npm update hexo-theme-butterfly</span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure><h1 id="Apply-Theme"><a href="#Apply-Theme" class="headerlink" title="Apply Theme"></a>Apply Theme</h1><p>Modify the Hexo root directory’s <code>_config.yml</code>, change the theme setting to <code>butterfly</code>:</p><figure class="highlight yaml"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line"><span class="attr">theme:</span> <span class="string">butterfly</span></span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure><h1 id="Install-Required-Plugins"><a href="#Install-Required-Plugins" class="headerlink" title="Install Required Plugins"></a>Install Required Plugins</h1><div class="tabs"><div class="nav-tabs"><button type="button" class="tab active">Renderer</button></div><div class="tab-contents"><div class="tab-item-content active"><p>If you have not yet installed the <code>pug</code> and <code>stylus</code> renderers, install them:</p><figure class="highlight bash"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line">npm install hexo-renderer-pug hexo-renderer-stylus --save</span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure></div></div><div class="tab-to-top"><button type="button" aria-label="scroll to top"><i class="fas fa-arrow-up"></i></button></div></div><h1 id="Upgrade-Recommendations"><a href="#Upgrade-Recommendations" class="headerlink" title="Upgrade Recommendations"></a>Upgrade Recommendations</h1><div class="note info flat"><p>To avoid losing custom configuration during theme upgrades, it is recommended to use <a href="https://hexo.io/docs/data-files.html">Hexo’s Data Files</a> feature.</p></div><p>Create a file <code>_config.butterfly.yml</code> in the Hexo root directory and copy the entire contents of the theme’s <code>_config.yml</code> into it.</p><blockquote><p>Please note that the content in <code>_config.butterfly.yml</code> will override the settings in <code>themes/butterfly/_config.yml</code>.<br>When updating the theme, check if the theme’s <code>_config.yml</code> has any new settings added, and copy them to <code>_config.butterfly.yml</code>.</p></blockquote><p><strong>Do NOT delete <code>themes/butterfly/_config.yml</code></strong>, it is still required by the theme even when using the override file.</p><figure class="highlight plaintext"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br><span class="line">4</span><br><span class="line">5</span><br><span class="line">6</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><span class="line">.</span><br><span class="line">├── _config.butterfly.yml   # Theme override config (your custom settings)</span><br><span class="line">├── _config.yml             # Hexo root config</span><br><span class="line">├── themes/</span><br><span class="line">│   └── butterfly/</span><br><span class="line">│       └── _config.yml     # Theme default config (do not delete)</span><br></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>Once <code>_config.butterfly.yml</code> exists, it takes priority over the theme’s own <code>_config.yml</code>.</p><div class="note success flat"><p>You are ready to start! Run <code>hexo server</code> to preview your blog locally.</p></div>]]>
